    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d688">

                <pb facs="0589" n="577" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg577"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.6363/25: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>)<anchor n="34" xml:id="d688-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-19T18:00:00+03:00">May 19, 1942—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 22—4:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>811. F. W. Ohliger, representative of Casoc at Dhahran, Saudi Arabia, is
                    proceeding Washington where he proposes to present to War Department certain
                    considerations relating to measures essential to the defense of the oil
                    properties in that country as well as eventual denial operations. From my
                    conversations with the Americans connected with Casoc and Bahrein Petroleum
                    Company, I am impressed with importance of these problems and I hope Department
                    will facilitate Ohliger’s representations to War Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d688-f1" n="34" type="source" xml:id="d688-f1-content">
                <p>Also accredited as Minister to Saudi Arabia.</p>
            </note>
